AWS DATA PROCESSING ADDENDUM
Amazon Web Services, Inc.

Effective Date: August 5, 2026
Customer: VisaCanada Inc.
AWS Account ID: [customer-account-id]
Services: Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service)

This Data Processing Addendum ("AWS DPA") is incorporated into the AWS Customer Agreement and governs the processing of Customer Content that constitutes Personal Data.

1. DEFINITIONS
   "Customer Content" means content that Customer or End Users transfer to AWS for processing, storage, or hosting.
   "Personal Data" means information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person.
   "AWS Content" means software, data, text, audio, video, or images provided by AWS.

2. SCOPE OF PROCESSING
   2.1 AWS will process Customer Content only to provide the Services and as instructed by Customer.
   2.2 Customer is the data controller; AWS is the data processor.
   2.3 This DPA applies to S3 buckets storing immigration documents in ca-central-1 region.

3. DATA PROTECTION OBLIGATIONS
   3.1 AWS will:
       - Implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures
       - Ensure AWS personnel process Personal Data only as necessary
       - Assist Customer in responding to data subject rights requests
       - Notify Customer of security breaches without undue delay
       - Delete or return Personal Data upon request or termination

4. SECURITY MEASURES
   4.1 Encryption:
       - At rest: AES-256 via S3 Server-Side Encryption (SSE-S3)
       - In transit: TLS 1.2 or higher for all API calls

   4.2 Access Controls:
       - AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)
       - Bucket policies restricting access to authorized principals
       - MFA required for sensitive operations

   4.3 Logging and Monitoring:
       - AWS CloudTrail enabled for all S3 API calls
       - S3 Access Logs enabled
       - AWS Config tracking configuration changes

   4.4 Compliance Certifications:
       - ISO 27001, 27017, 27018
       - SOC 1, SOC 2, SOC 3
       - PCI DSS Level 1
       - PIPEDA-equivalent controls in Canadian regions

5. DATA RESIDENCY
   5.1 Region: ca-central-1 (Montreal, Quebec, Canada)
   5.2 S3 Bucket Policy Configuration:
       ```json
       {
         "Version": "2012-10-17",
         "Statement": [
           {
             "Effect": "Deny",
             "Principal": "*",
             "Action": "s3:*",
             "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::visacanada-documents/*",
             "Condition": {
               "StringNotEquals": {
                 "aws:RequestedRegion": "ca-central-1"
               }
             }
           }
         ]
       }
       ```
   5.3 No cross-region replication enabled.
   5.4 All data processing occurs exclusively within ca-central-1.

6. SUBPROCESSORS
   6.1 AWS uses subprocessors listed at: https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/sub-processors/
   6.2 Customer will receive 30 days notice of new subprocessors via AWS notifications.

7. DATA SUBJECT RIGHTS
   7.1 AWS provides tools for Customer to fulfill data subject requests:
       - S3 API for data retrieval (GetObject)
       - S3 Object Tagging for data classification
       - S3 Lifecycle policies for automated deletion
       - S3 Inventory for data discovery

8. SECURITY BREACH NOTIFICATION
   8.1 AWS will notify Customer within 72 hours of becoming aware of a security breach affecting Customer Content.
   8.2 Notification channels:
       - AWS Security Hub
       - AWS Health Dashboard
       - Email to registered security contacts
   8.3 Notification includes:
       - Description of breach
       - Affected resources (bucket names, object keys)
       - AWS remediation actions
       - Recommended customer actions

9. AUDIT RIGHTS
   9.1 Customer may audit AWS compliance via:
       - AWS Artifact (compliance reports)
       - CloudTrail logs (API activity)
       - Third-party audit reports (SOC 2, ISO 27001)
   9.2 On-site audits available upon request (30 days notice, max once per year).

10. DATA RETENTION AND DELETION
    10.1 Customer controls retention via S3 Lifecycle policies.
    10.2 Upon termination or deletion request:
         - Objects deleted within 24 hours
         - Versioned copies deleted within 30 days
         - Backup copies deleted within 90 days
    10.3 Secure deletion: AWS uses NIST 800-88 media sanitization standards.

11. INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS
    11.1 No data transfers outside Canada without Customer authorization.
    11.2 If transfer required (e.g., customer-initiated), AWS ensures adequate safeguards (Standard Contractual Clauses).

12. LIABILITY AND INDEMNIFICATION
    Each party's liability is governed by the AWS Customer Agreement.

13. TERM AND TERMINATION
    13.1 Effective: August 5, 2026
    13.2 Expiration: August 5, 2027
    13.3 Auto-renewal: Yes, unless terminated with 60 days notice.

AGREED AND ACCEPTED:

